(2203067, 303681, 39484, '<td valign="top">Good job matching the eyes to the background.  Also the lighting is nice.  The depth of field is a little too shallow, so her right eye is a bit too soft. (Raise the aperture number)  If you shot more of a profile shot, the softness would not matter as much, but as it is sort of in the center, it attracts a lot if attention.   I''m not sure I agree with cropping her chin off.  I also think that you are shooting down on her too much.  Perhaps you could shoot more on her level.  This would also get rid of the large shoulder element on the left side.  One last thing, make sure you set the size to 640X640.  You are not using the full image size available to you.  Overall, nice tonal pallet.</td>', 'Good job matching the eyes to the background.  Also the lighting is nice.  The depth of field is a little too shallow, so her right eye is a bit too soft. (Raise the aperture number)  If you shot more of a profile shot, the softness would not matter as much, but as it is sort of in the center, it attracts a lot if attention.   I''m not sure I agree with cropping her chin off.  I also think that you are shooting down on her too much.  Perhaps you could shoot more on her level.  This would also get rid of the large shoulder element on the left side.  One last thing, make sure you set the size to 640X640.  You are not using the full image size available to you.  Overall, nice tonal pallet.', '2006-03-06 01:27:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(2203069, 303073, 4767, '<td valign="top">Really nice shot.  Reminds me of a series of calendar shots that Sam Haskins did for Pentax a few years ago.</td>', 'Really nice shot.  Reminds me of a series of calendar shots that Sam Haskins did for Pentax a few years ago.', '2006-03-06 01:28:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(2203070, 303270, 42005, '<td valign="top">This is a uniquely interesting photograph.   Somehow the color pulls my eye away from the rest of the photo. Perhaps that is your aim.   At any rate, I would love it on my wall without the item on the right.  The use of the wavy lines is very intriguing and pleasing on the eye.</td>', 'This is a uniquely interesting photograph.   Somehow the color pulls my eye away from the rest of the photo. Perhaps that is your aim.   At any rate, I would love it on my wall without the item on the right.  The use of the wavy lines is very intriguing and pleasing on the eye.', '2006-03-06 01:28:25.000000', NULL, 1),
