(2207520, 303543, 6999, '<td valign="top">Not bad. The depth of field is possibly a bit arbitrary - somehere in that region between deep and shallow, and might happily have been a bit more in either direction. I think I get your point with the composition, but I don''t think the thirds rule applies so strongly to a square crop, and the space a bottom of frame seems left there only to make the image square, rather than this set-up requiring a square crop to work, if you follow me.</td>', 'Not bad. The depth of field is possibly a bit arbitrary - somehere in that region between deep and shallow, and might happily have been a bit more in either direction. I think I get your point with the composition, but I don''t think the thirds rule applies so strongly to a square crop, and the space a bottom of frame seems left there only to make the image square, rather than this set-up requiring a square crop to work, if you follow me.', '2006-03-07 14:25:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(2207525, 303029, 34134, '<td valign="top">Don''t know what happened here, but the bottome 20% of the picture didn''t load.</td>', 'Don''t know what happened here, but the bottome 20% of the picture didn''t load.', '2006-03-07 14:26:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(2207531, 302744, 6999, '<td valign="top">decent enough detail, and focus, and so on, but to me simply an architectural portrait - telling me very little, affecting me likewise very little. Whilst the exposure is ''correct'' in the sense of nothing is over- and nothing is under-exposed, the overall brightness of this is taken too far: you''d get more impact, more sense of the true depth of colour of the stone, more drama to the shot if you were to lower the overall brightness level - just try adjusting with levels and moving the slider to the right a bit, just to give it some punch. A perfectly fine, ut an unexciting entry.</td>', 'decent enough detail, and focus, and so on, but to me simply an architectural portrait - telling me very little, affecting me likewise very little. Whilst the exposure is ''correct'' in the sense of nothing is over- and nothing is under-exposed, the overall brightness of this is taken too far: you''d get more impact, more sense of the true depth of colour of the stone, more drama to the shot if you were to lower the overall brightness level - just try adjusting with levels and moving the slider to the right a bit, just to give it some punch. A perfectly fine, ut an unexciting entry.', '2006-03-07 14:28:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(2207532, 301152, 43405, '<td valign="top">Could this be a LG composition perhaps? Excellent photograph, and nicely edited (possibly a bit too much sharpening). At least a top 10 finisher I think</td>', 'Could this be a LG composition perhaps? Excellent photograph, and nicely edited (possibly a bit too much sharpening). At least a top 10 finisher I think', '2006-03-07 14:29:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(2207533, 302618, 13879, '<td valign="top">My pick for Blue! Fantastic shot that really brought a smile to my face. I have my fingers crossed for you!!! 10</td>', 'My pick for Blue! Fantastic shot that really brought a smile to my face. I have my fingers crossed for you!!! 10', '2006-03-07 14:29:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2207536, 303271, 31443, '<td valign="top">Cute! Really sharp..</td>', 'Cute! Really sharp..', '2006-03-07 14:30:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2207537, 303322, 6999, '<td valign="top">Too much ice, not enough location/context? I don''t know if your idea ws to find interest in the light through the ice, but framing os closely the whole piece doesn''t work in that sense for me, and yet it''s so closely framed that I get no sense of location.</td>', 'Too much ice, not enough location/context? I don''t know if your idea ws to find interest in the light through the ice, but framing os closely the whole piece doesn''t work in that sense for me, and yet it''s so closely framed that I get no sense of location.', '2006-03-07 14:30:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(2207542, 303236, 6999, '<td valign="top">Quite fun. Good detail, great light, competent framing and so on. Selective de-sat always bothers me, I''m never quite sure why. Perhaps not taking the de- side of things to the full extreme might be more impactful without my feeling that my attention is being forced onto the hair when it would be there anyway? Not sure - I get the impact, sure, and I almost see the point, but I don''t like the level of - well, manipulation - it feels like I''m being subjected to.</td>', 'Quite fun. Good detail, great light, competent framing and so on. Selective de-sat always bothers me, I''m never quite sure why. Perhaps not taking the de- side of things to the full extreme might be more impactful without my feeling that my attention is being forced onto the hair when it would be there anyway? Not sure - I get the impact, sure, and I almost see the point, but I don''t like the level of - well, manipulation - it feels like I''m being subjected to.', '2006-03-07 14:32:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(2207551, 303388, 13879, '<td valign="top">Great shot! Hope it does well. Reminds me of the work of ''tony mendoza''. 10 from me</td>', 'Great shot! Hope it does well. Reminds me of the work of ''tony mendoza''. 10 from me', '2006-03-07 14:37:22.000000', NULL, 1),
