(2224011, 303452, 43405, '<td valign="top">IMHO, I really think that this shot does not do justice to the rest of your portfolio. While on a techical level I guess it is pretty good, but I''ve learned that very high keyish type photographs (which is often used to mask other imperfections) does not go down too well on DP. This just feels too harsh on the eyes.<br/> <br/>The composition just doesn''t do it for me. Difficult to read the photograph, and I can''t quite put my finger on it... but there almost feels as if there is something wrong with the photograph (hope I make sense).<br/> <br/>Love your other work though. <br/></td>', 'IMHO, I really think that this shot does not do justice to the rest of your portfolio. While on a techical level I guess it is pretty good, but I''ve learned that very high keyish type photographs (which is often used to mask other imperfections) does not go down too well on DP. This just feels too harsh on the eyes. The composition just doesn''t do it for me. Difficult to read the photograph, and I can''t quite put my finger on it... but there almost feels as if there is something wrong with the photograph (hope I make sense). Love your other work though. ', '2006-03-13 08:20:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2224042, 302840, 36078, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club:<br/> <br/>Congratulatons on a top 20 finish and for almost making the top 10.<br/> <br/>Very stunning image color balance wise.  The white or light colored background makes the rest of the colors pop right out.  Nice pose on the subject as well.  I myself would have liked to have seen the flowers the insect was perched on in a little more focus.  IE not such a shallow depth of field.  The size of the insect is perfect.  Perfectly placed as well within the frame.  I think it works perfectly for a square crop.  But ultimately I think people are tired of seeing macro insects.  Thats about the only reason i can think for you not to finish in the top 10 or even higher.</td>', 'From the Critique Club: Congratulatons on a top 20 finish and for almost making the top 10. Very stunning image color balance wise.  The white or light colored background makes the rest of the colors pop right out.  Nice pose on the subject as well.  I myself would have liked to have seen the flowers the insect was perched on in a little more focus.  IE not such a shallow depth of field.  The size of the insect is perfect.  Perfectly placed as well within the frame.  I think it works perfectly for a square crop.  But ultimately I think people are tired of seeing macro insects.  Thats about the only reason i can think for you not to finish in the top 10 or even higher.', '2006-03-13 08:48:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(2224079, 302351, 5885, '<td valign="top">Wow! You got "Rebeled" on the scores, that''s for sure. The level of competence in this photo far outweigh the scores it recieved.</td>', 'Wow! You got "Rebeled" on the scores, that''s for sure. The level of competence in this photo far outweigh the scores it recieved.', '2006-03-13 09:07:01.000000', NULL, 0),
